        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "With the current Neovim release schedule, this will happen in about two years (after possible 0.13.0 release). So I'll refrain from making such long term prediction :)\r\n\r\nThe advantages of current approach are that type checking errors neatly have `(mini.xxx)` prefix and it is even faster than the current Nightly fast `vim.validate()`. The disadvantage is that it requires 5 extra line per module (i.e. 200+ lines per 'mini.nvim'). Probably keeping current solution is fine, but we'll see.",
